+## One problem, three tools 🧰 {.smaller}
+
+*How many sequences are in my FASTA file?*
+
+**Bash** 🐚 (week 2)
+
+```bash
+grep -c ">" data/sequences.fasta
+```
+
+**Python** 🐍
+
+```python
+with open("data/sequences.fasta") as f:
+    print(sum(1 for line in f if line.startswith(">")))
+```
+
+**R** 🇷
+
+```r
+sum(startsWith(readLines("data/sequences.fasta"), ">"))
+```
+
+. . .
+
+Every language can solve the same problem. Each one has a place where it is the **easiest** 💛
+
+::: notes
+~3 min, just show it. Bash: quick one-off questions about files. Python: building tools.
+R: statistics and plots. No need to go deeper.
+:::
